prompt:
A real photograph, taken with a good phone camera and looking exactly like a phone photograph, of the dining room of a small neighbourhood restaurant in Berlin on an autumn evening, taken as a guest standing by the entrance a few metres away would take it, in a tall vertical picture, everything in sharp focus. Natural colours, warm light from the hanging lamps and the candles, the blue dusk in the window at the back. The textures of real dark wood, white linen, glass, ceramic, brass, paper, fabric and skin, with the true depth and the slight lens perspective of a photograph.

The first reference picture shows the young man from the front, the second in three-quarter view: his face, his short hair, his build and his height stay exactly as in them. Use them for the person only; his clothes here are a dark-green sweater over a white shirt whose collar shows, dark jeans and brown leather shoes.

Every object stands on its own, with a little space around it, so that the eye can tell at once where each thing is. Nothing in the picture carries any writing, numbers or print: the menu is a plain folded card of thick cream paper with no print, the waitress's notepad shows only blank paper, the bottles on the bar are plain dark glass with no labels, the wall clock has a plain face and no numbers, the picture on the wall is a plain landscape painting of a lake, and nothing in the room carries a sign, a logo, a brand or a chalkboard.

THE FRONT of the picture: a square table with a white tablecloth, seen from slightly above, with two wooden chairs. On the table, from the left of the picture to the right:
- a basket of bread rolls;
- a white plate with a knife on its right and a fork on its left, a soup spoon above it;
- a folded white cloth napkin beside the plate;
- a tall glass of water and a plain glass bottle of water;
- a lit white candle in a small brass holder;
- a single yellow flower in a small glass;
- a small salt shaker and a small pepper shaker side by side.

THE YOUNG MAN of the reference pictures sits at this table on the chair on the right, seen whole from his head to his shoes, which rest on the wooden floor under the table. He is caught in the very moment of ordering: he holds the open menu in the hand nearer the waitress and points with the index finger of his other hand at a line on it, looking up at the waitress with a friendly smile. His grey wool coat hangs over the back of his chair, and his black backpack stands on the floor beside the chair.

THE WAITRESS, a woman of about thirty-five with dark hair in a bun, in a white shirt and a long black apron, stands beside his table on the left and writes on a small notepad with a pen, leaning her head slightly towards him and smiling.

THE MIDDLE of the picture, on the right: a second table where an older couple is eating: a man of about sixty-five with grey hair and glasses, in a brown jacket, cuts a piece of meat on his plate with roast potatoes, and a woman of about sixty with short white hair, in a red cardigan, eats a bowl of soup; on their table a plate of fish with a slice of lemon, a green salad in a bowl, two glasses of red wine and a bottle of wine, and a small candle.

THE BACK of the picture:
- a dark wooden bar counter with a brass rail, on which stand a coffee machine, two white cups on saucers, and a cake under a glass dome on a cake stand;
- behind the counter, a shelf of wine bottles and beer bottles, all plain dark glass with no labels, and a row of hanging glasses;
- a waiter, a young man of about twenty-five in a white shirt and a black apron, carrying two plates of pizza towards a table, seen from the side;
- a tall window with a dark-red curtain pulled to one side, the blue evening sky and a street lamp outside;
- a round wall clock with a plain white face and no numbers above the bar;
- a framed painting of a lake in a plain wooden frame on the cream wall;
- a tall green plant in a pot in the corner by a wooden door;
- three warm hanging lamps with brass shades over the tables.
